    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** lineup for August 22nd is anchored by **Coby Mayo** (65.57) and **Gunnar Henderson** (63.26), who serve as our highest-upside plays despite a tough matchup against McClanahan. **Coby Mayo** benefits immensely from a favorable park factor (+16%) and a strong platoon advantage, making him an elite utility play. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a difficult southpaw, the high scoring output is driven by park dynamics that mitigate the platoon penalty. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.15) also remains a mandatory start; his raw power against Weathers keeps him in the upper echelon of our daily projections despite a neutral park environment.\n\nWe are keeping a close watch on **Jackson Merrill** (59.11) and **Kyle Tucker** (58.24), both of whom provide excellent efficiency. **Jackson Merrill** is a high-priority start due to his dual-threat potential\u2014his speed is vital to our pursuit of the scarcity-driven SB category, even with a minor efficiency hit from the opposing battery's ability to hold runners. **Sam Antonacci** (55.30) and **Miguel Vargas** (47.82) are both bolstered by favorable wind conditions at their venue, providing a boost to their base projection against Scott that keeps them ahead of the fringe options.\n\nThe most difficult decision of the day involved **Heliot Ramos** (45.34), who was the first player cut from our starting nine. While **Heliot Ramos** offers some upside against Cease, his current projection failed to eclipse the efficiency scores of our utility and middle infield slots. We continue to monitor the status of **Wade Meckler** and **Luis Robert Jr.**; as their lineups are currently pending, their projected scores are tethered to assumed batting order spots. Should either shift toward the bottom of the order, we may need to pivot to ensure our SB floor remains intact. We remain without **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**, who continue their recovery on the IL.",
